ado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Bruce F. Young | President, CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $957,213 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $257K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $11K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Concrete Pumping Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $479M market cap on $393M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding. Operating margins are expanding by +4.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 41%.","The business throws off $18M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 10.09\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 14.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 28% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4252606.26},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 53% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 32% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(BBCP) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/BBCP_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_103126022802_1793428082.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793428082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are Investors Undervaluing Concrete Pumping Holdings (BBCP) Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3018322/are-investors-undervaluing-concrete-pump